# Local host-port overrides for the simple-poll demo — copy to docker/.env.
#
# Compose reads a `.env` from THIS directory (docker/) before any container
# exists and uses it to interpolate the ${VAR:-default} host-port publishes in
# docker-compose.local.yml. This is NOT the container env_file — that is the
# demo's ../.env, which only reaches container environments. A host-port value
# set in ../.env is silently ignored; set it here to actually move the port.
#
# docker/.env is gitignored (host-specific). Leave it absent, or leave a knob
# below commented, and compose keeps the default shown — no setup step is needed
# on a fresh clone. Uncomment and change a knob to republish that service on a
# different host port (e.g. to dodge a port already taken on this host).

# Daemon status / worker-comm / websocket, published to the host (shifted per
# demo so stacks coexist; simple-poll owns 8104-8106):
# HTTP_STATUS_HOST_PORT=8104
# WORKER_COMM_HOST_PORT=8105
# WEBSOCKET_HOST_PORT=8106

# MySQL, phpMyAdmin, nginx HTTPS, and the Angular dev server:
# MYSQL_HOST_PORT=33065
# PHPMYADMIN_PORT=8082
# NGINX_HTTPS_PORT=8445
# FRONTEND_DEV_PORT=5175
